Refuse the end-of-generation token while a reasoning block is open.

Mistral Small 4 sometimes emits its end-of-sequence token after "[THINK]"
and before "[/THINK]" (about 1-2% of thinking-mode replies, 8% on one
recorded coding chat). The reply ends with finish_reason "stop", so the
server files everything the model wrote, often a finished answer, under
reasoning and the client sees no answer. The model's probability for the
token is tiny at those points (about 0.01%, while "[/THINK]" has 97-99.8%),
so masking it changes the model's other choices very little.

The reasoning-budget sampler already tracks when a reasoning block is open
(from the chat template's start and end tags, and from the generation
prompt). This adds a list of tokens it masks to -inf while the block is
open. The server and CLI fill it with every end-of-generation token when
"--reasoning-block-eog" (env LLAMA_ARG_REASONING_BLOCK_EOG) or the request
field "reasoning_block_eog" is set. Unlike a grammar, this also works for
requests that have tools (a request grammar is rejected with tools, and the
server-wide grammar is replaced by the tool-call grammar). Default off.

Apply to llama.cpp v0.8.0 with "patch -p1".

AI Disclosure:
- Authorship: Autonomous
- Models: claude-sonnet-5-5 (Anthropic)
- Scope: Wrote this patch so Mistral Small 4 replies cannot end inside the
  thinking block, as the user asked after the grammar test showed the
  approach but could not cover requests with tools.
- References: https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp (v0.8.0, common/reasoning-budget.cpp)

